   246	
   247	Suppose first that the graph contains some unlocated components, and we show how to deal with them.
   248	We want to find one edge $p_ip_{i+1}$ of $T'$ which we can subdivide many times and place all
   249	unlocated components in between of $p_i$ and $p_{i+1}$ in $T$. We call an edge $p_ip_{i+1}$
