The generic reference now solves all eight audited shipping seeds in exactly 43 Algorithm X nodes, after 1,764 pair candidates; counted work ranges from about 9,000 to 21,000 primitive checks per instance. That is a much cleaner Track B claim: mechanically easy for code, plainly impractical to execute by hand, while the residue invariant stays under the 300-operation cap. I’m running the full 200,000-sample gate suite next.
