    70	Extend this partial interval representation in its fixed host path.
    71	
    72	Definitions.
    73	A subpath [a,b] is the nonempty set of host vertices p_a,p_(a+1),...,p_b, with integer endpoints 0 <= a <= b.
    74	An interval representation assigns one subpath to every graph vertex; two distinct graph vertices must be adjacent exactly when their assigned subpaths intersect.
    75	The host path is fixed: it may not be subdivided and no vertices or branches may be added.
    76	
    77	Here n=2 and M=122412. The fixed host path has vertices p_0 through p_244826.
    78	The graph is the disjoint union of split vertices s_0,...,s_2 and 6 take components T_0,...,T_5.
