    80	Take component T_i is a path with A_i edges and labelled graph vertices x_(i,0),...,x_(i,A_i); its A_i is listed below. No vertex of a take component is pre-drawn.
    81	Thus gap g is the M host vertices strictly between s_g and s_(g+1), namely coordinates (M+1)g+1 through (M+1)g+M, inclusive.
    82	
    83	Output a compact placement matrix with one row [g,r] for each T_i, in increasing i order. Here g is its 0-based gap and r is its 0-based left-to-right rank in that gap.
