codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track B generator based on the paper’s Theorem 3 reduction from 3-PARTITION to fixed-path interval-representation extension. It is honestly classified as a paper-licensed reduction, not full native-domain coverage. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0255)

Key results:

- All local gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 each.
- Generic Algorithm X reference: 8/8, 107,120 operations and 344 nodes total.
- G9(c): 853 characters, 252 atoms, 254 intended operations.
- 200 additional shipping seeds built and verified deterministically.

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/gen_1207_0255.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only incomplete requirement is the external four-vendor verdict: every bare, hinted, and placebo call returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The transcripts preserve those errors, and none are misreported as model failures. A funded OpenRouter key is required before submission; this is not a rejection of the family or paper.
