codex
Implemented and verified the Track B generator based on the paper’s Theorem 3 fixed-path interval-extension reduction.

Key results:

- Shipping preset: `medium`, `n=30`
- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass
- Guessing: 0/200,000
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 each
- Bare oracle loop: `easy` solved; `medium` held 0/3
- Answer size: 601 characters, 180 atoms
- Intended route: at most 182 exact operations

Deliverables:

- [gen_1207_0255.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/gen_1207_0255.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.0255/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

One non-gating diagnostic remains incomplete: OpenRouter quota was exhausted after 2/3 hinted attempts and before any placebo attempt completed. Errors are preserved and not counted as model failures. The repository hardener’s currently configured pool also contained two vendors rather than the four described in the task.
